+# Corpus fetching
+
+The corpus fetch recorded the following per-domain limit:
+
+- **Visits:** 12
+- **Window:** 60 seconds
+- **Cooldown after a breach:** 900 seconds (15 minutes)
+
+The fetch used these source/CDN or mirror hosts:
+
+- `raw.githubusercontent.com`
+- `cdn.jsdelivr.net` (using `/gh/<owner>/<repo>@<branch>/<path>` URLs)
+- `cdn.statically.io`
+
+`cdn.statically.io` was observed to be slow and to time out. Later fetch batches
+were kept to at most 12 visits per domain, spaced by at least 65 seconds, and
+alternated between the raw GitHub and jsDelivr hosts.
+
+These values come from the project's recorded fetch session. The checked-in
+corpus itself independently confirms `raw.githubusercontent.com` in
+`manifest.tsv`, but this checkout contains neither the fetch script nor a raw
+request log with which to independently verify the numeric limits or the two
+mirror hosts.
